-- title:
--   Supersingular valuation ring with base-layer stalks, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. A *rigid-level guard* consists of a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   The geometric data at level $M'$ over the residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` are: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`) over $\kappa$, which by `hW` is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' κ` of supersingular places, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) \in$ `ssJSet q κ`; a distinguished element $s \in W$; the hypothesis `hle` that the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of the full level-$M'$ function field is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the unit-group reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with residue target `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a `ConstantReduction`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \kappa$, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with orders); and the hypothesis `hR₀` that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A \to \kappa$.
--
--   The *small constants* are an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, subject to: $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`: every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0 \cap A$ with $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   The *auxiliary level data* are a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   The *base layer of constants* consists of an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$, and a nonzero $\varpi_b \in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   With $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, the assertion is the existence of an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following nine properties.
--
--   (1) $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_0 =$ `fieldBar q M'`: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the range of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'` is everything.
--
--   (2) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (4) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) There is $t \in W_0$ which is residually transcendental in the following sense: for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then the image in $W_0$ of every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (6) For every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and which satisfies both: at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$ (regularity of $g$ wherever $j$ is regular, $j$ being the image of `jq`); and the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$ — the image of $g$ under the inclusion `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (7) For every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $F_0$ into $F_0$, and for $f \in F_0$ whose image also lies in $F_0$, $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (8) Linear disjointness over $k_0$: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, then $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   (9) For every field $FSS$ equipped with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with residue target $FSS$ (a `RegularProlongation`: a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, with a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \kappa$, and satisfying the scaling condition), such that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f \in W_0$, two conclusions hold.
--
--   (9a) Identification of the special fibre as a Drinfeld quotient: for every $\kappa$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ over $\mathbb F_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2`, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e : FSS \cong$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the $C_s$-action) such that $\#C_s = 2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, where `placeWidthChar` is `jWidthChar q (s.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M'))` divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`, and such that the level automorphisms act through the Drinfeld $H$-action: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, given that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), one has for all $x \in FSS$ the equality, inside [`DrinfeldCurve.drinfeldFunctionField q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L12), of $e$ applied to $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` at $x$ with [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $e(x)$.
--
--   (9b) Base-layer smooth-point stalks: there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$ with $\#N = q+1$, and families, indexed by places $Q$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, of subrings $S_b(Q)$ of `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_b(Q) : A_b[X] \to S_b(Q)$ and $\chi_b(Q) : S_b(Q) \to \kappa$, and sets $D_b(Q)$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that for every $Q \notin N$: the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_b(Q)$; $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a)$ is that image; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(X)) = 0$; $S_b(Q)$ is a local ring whose maximal ideal is the kernel of $\chi_b(Q)$; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element $f$ of that join can be written with $f\,h = g$ for some $g,h \in S_b(Q)$ with $h \ne 0$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and of essentially finite type; every element of $S_b(Q)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and such an element lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if it is divisible by $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,\varpi_b)$; for every $f \in S_b(Q)$, the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in $Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is the image of $\chi_b(Q)(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_b(Q)(X)$ has $Q$-order equal to $1$; and $D_b(Q)$ consists exactly of the places $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that are rational, for which every $f \in S_b(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for which $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ precisely when $\chi_b(Q)(f) = 0$.
--
--   Moreover, in (9b): the discs are disjoint, in the sense that if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some place $P$ lies in both $D_b(Q)$ and $D_b(Q')$ then $Q = Q'$; for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_b(Q)$ one has $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $j$ in `fieldBar q M'`; and the whole configuration is equivariant for the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$: for every $\tau$ in that subgroup preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every place $Q$, the place $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q$ lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does, and if $Q \notin N$ then $\{P \mid \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_b(Q)\} = D_b(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q)$.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ form, with the rigid-level guard $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $\ell_g \mid M'$, of the construction of the valuation ring attached to a supersingular point on the stable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$, together with the stalks of its base layer at the smooth points of the special fibre: the special fibre is identified with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve of level $q$, compatibly with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms, and the $q+1$ excluded places mark the points where the supersingular annuli meet. It is obtained by combining the affine-chart construction [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd) with the two prolongation statements `supersingularProlongation_existDL_of_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd` and `supersingularProlongation_ends_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd` (the domain hypothesis on the Drinfeld coordinate ring coming from [`DrinfeldCurve.isDomain_coordRing_of_ne_one`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.isDomain_coordRing_of_ne_one)), and feeds the assembly of the full stable model in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
